1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:02,400
Hello everyone.

2
00:00:02,400 --> 00:00:10,140
Today's podcast topic is "With Friends vs. Alone."

3
00:00:10,140 --> 00:00:14,220
Do you guys like being alone?

4
00:00:14,220 --> 00:00:19,320
Or do you like being with friends?

5
00:00:19,320 --> 00:00:23,550
For me, it depends on the situation.

6
00:00:23,550 --> 00:00:26,840
It depends.

7
00:00:26,840 --> 00:00:31,340
There are some interesting words in Korea.

8
00:00:31,340 --> 00:00:36,410
They are "Hon-bap" and "Hon-gong."

9
00:00:36,410 --> 00:00:39,650
"Hon-bap" means eating alone,

10
00:00:39,650 --> 00:00:42,660
and what do you think "Hon-gong" is?

11
00:00:42,660 --> 00:00:47,510
"Hon-gong" means studying alone.

12
00:00:47,510 --> 00:00:49,270
They are abbreviations.

13
00:00:49,270 --> 00:00:55,260
So, some restaurants have signs like this.

14
00:00:55,260 --> 00:00:59,910
"Hon-bap Restaurant." What does this mean?

15
00:00:59,910 --> 00:01:05,900
It means you can go alone and order just one portion.

16
00:01:05,900 --> 00:01:14,840
In restaurants, when ordering food, we use the word "in-bun" (portion/serving).

17
00:01:14,840 --> 00:01:18,110
Since it's one person, it's 1-in-bun (one serving),

18
00:01:18,110 --> 00:01:21,630
if it's two people, 2-in-bun (two servings).

19
00:01:21,630 --> 00:01:24,960
If it's 3 people, how many servings is it?

20
00:01:24,960 --> 00:01:27,820
Yes, it's 3-in-bun (three servings).

21
00:01:27,820 --> 00:01:34,870
Here it says, "Solo customers are also welcome."

22
00:01:34,870 --> 00:01:39,880
"Go-gaek" is a polite way to say customer.

23
00:01:39,880 --> 00:01:42,570
Son-nim, Go-gaek.

24
00:01:42,570 --> 00:01:46,140
"Hwan-yeong-ham-ni-da" means Welcome.

25
00:01:46,140 --> 00:01:55,460
Usually, restaurant owners prefer it when many people come and order a lot of food.

26
00:01:55,460 --> 00:02:02,320
So, there are some restaurants where you can't eat alone.

27
00:02:02,320 --> 00:02:10,020
But the restaurant in this picture says, "Eating alone is also welcome."

28
00:02:10,020 --> 00:02:14,400
"It's okay for a customer to come alone."

29
00:02:14,400 --> 00:02:19,990
"It's okay to order just one serving," it says.

30
00:02:19,990 --> 00:02:28,190
These days in Korea, there are many people who eat alone and study alone.

31
00:02:28,190 --> 00:02:33,450
Restaurants have spaces that look like this.

32
00:02:33,450 --> 00:02:34,510
Space.

33
00:02:34,510 --> 00:02:39,620
In Japan, things like this are very common, right?

34
00:02:39,620 --> 00:02:40,940
To be common.

35
00:02:40,940 --> 00:02:42,290
It's common, right?

36
00:02:42,290 --> 00:02:47,540
In Korea, a lot of them have been popping up especially recently.

37
00:02:47,540 --> 00:02:50,300
They are popping up.

38
00:02:50,300 --> 00:02:58,160
But people have different thoughts on this "eating alone."

39
00:02:58,160 --> 00:03:02,350
People talk about it a lot on the internet.

40
00:03:02,350 --> 00:03:10,240
Some people say, "I can't eat alone. It's too embarrassing."

41
00:03:10,240 --> 00:03:13,360
But other people say,

42
00:03:13,360 --> 00:03:15,230
"Why can't you even do that?"

43
00:03:15,230 --> 00:03:19,340
"You can't eat at a restaurant alone?"

44
00:03:19,340 --> 00:03:20,990
"Are you a baby?"

45
00:03:20,990 --> 00:03:24,220
"Are you a little kid? A kid?"

46
00:03:24,220 --> 00:03:26,420
They say things like this.

47
00:03:26,420 --> 00:03:31,380
Like this, people's opinions are different.

48
00:03:31,380 --> 00:03:32,580
Opinion.

49
00:03:32,580 --> 00:03:35,020
Opinions are different.

50
00:03:35,020 --> 00:03:40,450
So eating alone is an interesting topic in Korea.

51
00:03:40,450 --> 00:03:43,010
How about you guys?

52
00:03:43,010 --> 00:03:50,910
To be honest... when I was young, I couldn't eat alone.

53
00:03:50,910 --> 00:03:58,560
But after I became an adult, I changed a lot.

54
00:03:58,560 --> 00:04:01,950
I became an independent person.

55
00:04:01,950 --> 00:04:07,890
It's a slightly difficult word, but a very commonly used expression.

56
00:04:07,890 --> 00:04:09,090
Independence.

57
00:04:09,090 --> 00:04:10,910
To be independent.

58
00:04:10,910 --> 00:04:21,240
An independent person does well on their own even without the help of parents or friends.

59
00:04:21,240 --> 00:04:25,390
It feels like a free cat.

60
00:04:25,390 --> 00:04:35,690
Dogs constantly follow their owners around, but cats play well on their own, right?

61
00:04:35,690 --> 00:04:39,930
Cats are independent animals.

62
00:04:39,930 --> 00:04:45,860
Anyway, after becoming an adult, I'm good at eating alone.

63
00:04:45,860 --> 00:04:52,640
And I also went on a trip alone for the first time.

64
00:04:52,640 --> 00:04:57,410
I went to a place called Gyeongju in Korea.

65
00:04:57,410 --> 00:05:02,780
Last year, I also went to Egypt alone.

66
00:05:02,780 --> 00:05:10,520
Later, I'll tell you guys a lot of my "solo travel" stories too.

67
00:05:10,520 --> 00:05:17,640
But originally, Korean people also really love doing things together.

68
00:05:17,640 --> 00:05:23,800
Especially young students like studying together.

69
00:05:23,800 --> 00:05:29,000
In Korea, there are places called "Study Cafes."

70
00:05:29,000 --> 00:05:33,760
They are quiet spaces for studying.

71
00:05:33,760 --> 00:05:39,840
We shorten "Study Cafe" and call it "Seu-ka."

72
00:05:39,840 --> 00:05:48,100
They are so popular that there are actually three of them near my house.

73
00:05:48,100 --> 00:05:50,210
There are as many as three.

74
00:05:50,210 --> 00:05:56,240
Speaking of which, I suddenly want to go.

75
00:05:56,240 --> 00:06:04,010
Anyway, there are many people who study here together with their friends.

76
00:06:04,010 --> 00:06:09,430
In the past, people studied a lot at the library.

77
00:06:09,430 --> 00:06:15,810
But these days, people go to study cafes, "Seu-ka."

78
00:06:15,810 --> 00:06:24,010
Also, people go to regular cafes a whole lot, not just "Seu-ka."

79
00:06:24,010 --> 00:06:30,000
They go to Starbucks or local cafes to study.

80
00:06:30,000 --> 00:06:36,890
Actually, for me... I can concentrate best at home.

81
00:06:36,890 --> 00:06:41,820
Cafes are too loud.

82
00:06:41,820 --> 00:06:49,600
Cafes are great when having delicious drinks or talking with a friend.

83
00:06:49,600 --> 00:06:53,660
But when it comes to studying,

84
00:06:53,660 --> 00:06:59,070
when it comes to studying, home is the best.

85
00:06:59,070 --> 00:07:04,560
On the contrary, my older sister absolutely!

86
00:07:04,560 --> 00:07:08,700
She absolutely likes doing things together.

87
00:07:08,700 --> 00:07:14,560
She studies with friends and eats with friends.

88
00:07:14,560 --> 00:07:22,170
So if she wants to learn something, the first thing she does is register at an academy.

89
00:07:22,170 --> 00:07:23,280
Registration.

90
00:07:23,280 --> 00:07:28,470
She says she wants to study together with people.

91
00:07:28,470 --> 00:07:39,680
When I was young, being with friends was so much fun that I couldn't study.

92
00:07:39,680 --> 00:07:46,110
When I was in high school, I went to the library with my friends.

93
00:07:46,110 --> 00:07:52,310
We went there to study, but we just kept eating.

94
00:07:52,310 --> 00:07:56,380
We ate snacks, ate tteokbokki...

95
00:07:56,380 --> 00:08:01,220
So... we couldn't study at all.

96
00:08:01,220 --> 00:08:02,750
Really!

97
00:08:02,750 --> 00:08:07,300
But now I understand my sister.

98
00:08:07,300 --> 00:08:08,900
I understand.

99
00:08:08,900 --> 00:08:13,980
Lately, my thoughts have changed a lot.

100
00:08:13,980 --> 00:08:21,470
Seeing other people working hard motivates me.

101
00:08:21,470 --> 00:08:23,010
To be motivated.

102
00:08:23,010 --> 00:08:24,380
For example,

103
00:08:24,380 --> 00:08:30,450
until now... I used to do home workouts at home.

104
00:08:30,450 --> 00:08:31,360
"Home-t" (Home workout).

105
00:08:31,360 --> 00:08:34,380
You've heard this expression before, right?

106
00:08:34,380 --> 00:08:39,370
But a few months ago, I registered at a gym.

107
00:08:39,370 --> 00:08:40,950
I registered.

108
00:08:40,950 --> 00:08:51,130
And I understood, "Ah, this is why people do things together."

109
00:08:51,130 --> 00:08:58,850
When you go to the gym, you can see other people working out.

110
00:08:58,850 --> 00:09:03,200
Seeing that really motivates me.

111
00:09:03,200 --> 00:09:13,950
"Ja-geuk-doen-da" means seeing someone else and getting the energy to think, "I should work hard too."

112
00:09:13,950 --> 00:09:16,150
How about you guys?

113
00:09:16,150 --> 00:09:24,610
Especially when studying a language, isn't it really lonely when studying Korean?

114
00:09:24,610 --> 00:09:29,150
I am also studying languages right now.

115
00:09:29,150 --> 00:09:33,720
I am studying Chinese and Japanese by myself.

116
00:09:33,720 --> 00:09:34,950
Self-study.

117
00:09:34,950 --> 00:09:40,890
Everything is good, but there is one thing that's a bit disappointing.

118
00:09:40,890 --> 00:09:44,230
I have no one to talk to.

119
00:09:44,230 --> 00:09:52,220
And even if I make sentences, I don't know if they are correct.

120
00:09:52,220 --> 00:09:57,290
I don't know if I'm pronouncing things well.

121
00:09:57,290 --> 00:10:09,700
So, for those who feel lonely studying alone, I created a small Korean group class.

122
00:10:09,700 --> 00:10:14,430
It's a Korean class where four people study together.

123
00:10:14,430 --> 00:10:20,100
It's a class where we study together like real friends.

124
00:10:20,100 --> 00:10:26,570
It's a class based on these slow podcasts.

125
00:10:26,570 --> 00:10:32,610
You can learn the expressions from the videos in more detail.

126
00:10:32,610 --> 00:10:39,040
And you can tell your own stories using those expressions.

127
00:10:39,040 --> 00:10:47,840
You can practice speaking Korean with friends.

128
00:10:47,840 --> 00:10:50,720
We motivate each other.

129
00:10:50,720 --> 00:10:52,320
Motivation!

130
00:10:52,320 --> 00:10:56,480
If we study together, you'll improve really fast.

131
00:10:56,480 --> 00:11:00,540
I will help you right by your side.

132
00:11:00,540 --> 00:11:08,250
I will teach you natural, real Korean sentences.

133
00:11:08,250 --> 00:11:11,140
We will also play Korean games.

134
00:11:11,140 --> 00:11:17,770
Those who feel lonely studying Korean! Let's do it together.

135
00:11:17,770 --> 00:11:20,430
Please check the link!

136
00:11:20,430 --> 00:11:25,590
Everyone, it's almost March.

137
00:11:25,590 --> 00:11:28,270
It's already March.

138
00:11:28,270 --> 00:11:38,390
In Korea, March means a new beginning, spring, a new semester.

139
00:11:38,390 --> 00:11:47,980
Korean elementary schools, middle schools, and universities all start fresh in March.

140
00:11:47,980 --> 00:11:53,920
Does March have that kind of meaning in your country too?

141
00:11:53,920 --> 00:11:57,700
I wonder if it's only like that in Korea.

142
00:11:57,700 --> 00:12:02,110
Please let me know your stories in the comments too.

143
00:12:02,110 --> 00:12:06,460
I read all the comments.

144
00:12:06,460 --> 00:12:10,460
Then, let's meet again in the next podcast.

145
00:12:10,460 --> 00:12:20,760
Bye!
